  "premise_review": [
    "Keep C : Type u with Category.{v} C and Presheaf.{u,v,w} exactly. No concrete category, presheaf or sheaf/descent proof is constructed here.",
    "Diagnostic contains a supplied presheaf plus ObservableField presheaf.F Nat and ObservableField presheaf.F String. It contains no severity order, status policy, acceptance flag, receipt hash or execution mechanism.",
    "The complete727-byte captured Observable provider was read: value is ∀ U, F.obj(op U) → α and naturality is an actual equality proof type value U (F.map f.op s) = value V s, for every restriction f and section s. It is not merely a Prop label lacking a proof field.",
    "Diagnostic.restrict is exactly the original presheaf restriction function for the supplied f : U ⟶ V and section over V; its result is a section over U.",
    "severity_natural requires X, the same f and s, and only applies X.severity.naturality f s. It neither derives a new observable field nor supplies any global diagnostic value.",
    "The status field likewise requires its own ObservableField data, but no separate status theorem or meaning for any status string is added.",
    "All3 source commands, dependent section/arrow types, u/v/w context, restrictions and equality/proof bytes are exact copies. Added open Folder.Sheaf explicitly restores the old ancestor lookup after namespace rebinding; compatibility remains unreplayed."
  ],
